## SECTION 3 â€” Important Improvements

### IMP-1: Chunking Strategy Strips All Punctuation and Lowercases Text

> **Issue**: The `clean_text()` function aggressively strips punctuation and lowercases everything, destroying semantic meaning.

**Evidence from code**:
- [data_preprocessing.py L21-25](../apps/embedding-service/modules/chunking/data_preprocessing.py#L21):
  ```python
  def clean_text(text):
      text = re.sub(r'[^\w\s]', '', text)  # removes ALL punctuation
      text = re.sub(r'\s+', ' ', text)
      text = re.sub(r'notice\s*disclaimer', 'Notice:\n\nDisclaimer:', text, flags=re.IGNORECASE)
      return text.lower()
  ```

**Why this is a problem**:
- Removes periods, commas, colons, hyphens â€” destroying sentence structure
- "ISO 27001" becomes "iso 27001", "$1,500" becomes "1500", "Q3-2025" becomes "q32025"
- The embedding model (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) handles raw text well â€” aggressive cleaning hurts more than helps
- The LLM receives mangled text without proper sentence structure, contributing to lower-quality answers

**Impact**: Degraded embedding quality, degraded LLM generation quality.

**Recommended Fix**: Only normalize whitespace. Preserve punctuation, case, and special characters. The embedding model and LLM are both trained on natural text.

**Priority**: P1  
**Estimated effort**: 30 minutes  
**Risk**: Requires re-embedding all existing documents.

