## SECTION 7 â€” What Would I Do Differently?

### Parts I Would Keep (Already Industry Quality)

| Component | Why It's Good |
|-----------|---------------|
| **Microservice architecture with gRPC** | Clean service boundaries. Python for ML, Node for API, React for UI. The gRPC choice is correct for inter-service communication. |
| **Provider abstraction pattern** | The `BaseLLMProvider` â†’ `get_provider()` factory is textbook clean. Adding new LLM providers requires zero changes to business logic. This is excellent. |
| **Modular prompt templates** | Separating system, grounding, formatting, citation, and refusal into individual files is the right approach. Easy to iterate without code changes. |
| **Trust Score system** | Multi-factor trust scoring (duplicate penalty, contradiction penalty, review freshness, document age) is sophisticated and enterprise-appropriate. |
| **Duplicate + Contradiction detection pipeline** | Three-level duplicate detection (hash â†’ full-text embedding â†’ chunk-level) is thorough. LLM-powered contradiction checking is genuinely advanced. |
| **Structured logging with Winston** | Domain-specific loggers (upload, chat, request) with daily rotation and correlation IDs is production-grade logging. |
| **Document ingestion with OCR** | Multi-format extraction (PDF, DOCX, PPTX, images) with fallback OCR is comprehensive. |

### Parts I Would Redesign

| Component | Current | What I'd Do | Why |
|-----------|---------|-------------|-----|
| **Prompt construction** | String concatenation with sentinel splitting | Build messages array directly in response_generator, pass structured messages to providers | Eliminates the fragile sentinel split entirely |
| **Context formatting** | Flat `\n`-joined text | XML-tagged sources with metadata per chunk | Gives the LLM structured context to work with |
| **Chunking** | Aggressive clean_text â†’ paragraph-based split | Recursive text splitter with semantic boundaries (section headers, paragraph breaks), minimal cleaning | Preserves document structure |
| **Retrieval pipeline** | Embedding â†’ Pinecone â†’ keyword boost â†’ diversity cap | Embedding â†’ Pinecone (topK=20) â†’ cross-encoder rerank â†’ dynamic top-N selection | Significantly better relevance |
| **Memory/History** | Flat string appended to prompt | Structured conversation history as separate message turns in the chat completion | Models handle multi-turn conversations natively |
| **Error responses to LLM** | Return generic error string | Return error via gRPC status codes | Proper error semantics |
| **Few-shot feedback loop** | File-based JSON on 10-minute cron | Event-driven (on feedback submission), stored in DB, loaded on demand | Real-time learning, no stale data |

